abstract:
Background Urolithin A (UA) is a metabolite produced by gut bacteria following the consumption of ellagitannin-rich foods. Clinical trials in middle-aged and older adults demonstrated that supplementation with UA improves muscle strength, endurance, and biomarkers of mitochondrial health, suggesting that UA may be an effective ergogenic aid in other populations. Methods In this double-blind, parallel group, placebo-controlled clinical trial ( NCT04783207 ), competitive male distance runners ( n = 42, 27.2 ± 1.0 years, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
